# Registered/full Quake game data is copyrighted and personal to each
# user's own purchase - don't commit it. The shareware pak0.pak is fine
# (see README) and stays tracked. Anchored to the root only - a mod's
# own pak1.pak (e.g. mods/fq/pak1.pak, a free fan mod's own assets) is
# unrelated and should stay tracked.
/pak1.pak
/pak2.pak
/pak3.pak

# Mod pak files that are too large for a normal git push (GitHub hard-rejects
# any file over 100MB without Git LFS, which this repo doesn't use) -- each
# deploy copies these in locally, same as the base game's own pak1.pak above.
# ad_start.bsp (extracted loose from mods/ad/pak1.pak, ~12MB) stays tracked --
# it's small and needed to disambiguate from the hub's own "start" map key.
/mods/ad/pak0.pak
/mods/ad/pak1.pak
/mods/ad/pak2.pak
/mods/quoth/pak1.pak

# User accounts/sessions database (password hashes) and TLS keys -- never commit.
/server/data/
/server/*.pem
